WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/feedback/NavigationGuardProvider.tsx — an in-app unsaved-changes navigation
  guard. A React context provider that owns a `Map<id, GuardEntry>` of "this form is dirty"
  callbacks, exposes `register(entry) -> unregister` and `confirmIfDirty() -> Promise<boolean>`,
  intercepts browser back/forward (popstate) when a guard is dirty, and renders a warning
  `<ConfirmDialog>` ("Unsaved changes"). Hooks: useId, useTranslation, useNavigate, useLocation,
  useNavigationGuardContext. Shared component: @/components/ui/ConfirmDialog.
  Branches reproduced (every one):
    • register(entry)            : registry.set(id, entry) → returns an unregister token (web cleanup fn)
    • findDirty()                : the first registered guard reporting dirty, in registration order
    • confirmIfDirty()           : no dirty ⇒ resolve(true); a dirty guard ⇒ show prompt, resolve to choice
    • pendingPromiseRef re-use   : a second racing caller awaits the SAME in-flight prompt (no stacking)
    • ConfirmDialog props        : variant="warning", silenceKey="unsaved-navigation",
                                   title forms.unsavedTitle, message pending?.message ?? forms.unsavedWarning,
                                   confirm forms.discard, cancel forms.keepEditing
    • silence ("Don't ask again"): honored for warning + silenceKey ⇒ when silenced, confirmIfDirty
                                   auto-proceeds without a dialog; ticking + discard persists the action
    • popstate handler           : no dirty ⇒ allow back; dirty ⇒ intercept + confirm; on discard replay back
    • resolve(ok)                : onConfirm ⇒ true (discard/navigate) · onCancel/backdrop ⇒ false (keep)
    • useNavigationGuardContext  : returns the context or NOOP_CTX (register inert, confirm proceeds)

