PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind/DOM ported)
  React Context + Provider               → @Environment(\.navigationGuard) + @MainActor @Observable
                                           NavigationGuardCoordinator; default = NoopNavigationGuardContext (NOOP_CTX).
  Promise<boolean> confirmIfDirty        → `func confirmIfDirty() async -> Bool` over CheckedContinuation(s);
                                           pendingPromiseRef re-use = a shared continuation list resolved once.
  <ConfirmDialog variant="warning">      → dimmed-scrim centered card + warning-tinted triangle icon + message box;
                                           Discard is `.destructive` (Apple HIG for discarding edits), Keep editing
                                           is the `.cancel`-style secondary; backdrop tap = keep editing (web onClose).
  silenceKey + confirmSilence            → @MainActor NavigationGuardSilence seam (.standard = UserDefaults allowlist
                                           teslasync:confirm-silence:v1, the peer ConfirmDialog store shape); "Don't
                                           ask again" toggle + auto-proceed.
  useNavigate / useLocation (popstate)   → NavigationGuardBackIntent + coordinator.confirmBack(); the host nav layer
                                           awaits it (the view does ZERO I/O — web parity).
  useId                                  → caller-supplied stable NavigationGuardEntry.id (the .navigationGuard modifier).
  Tailwind colors/spacing/radius         → Color.TS.* / TSSpacing / TSRadius / Font.TS (generated P1/S9 tokens).
  Button / Toggle / icons                → TSButton(.secondary/.destructive) · SwiftUI Toggle(.switch) ·
                                           SF Symbols (exclamationmark.triangle.fill, checkmark.shield, etc.).
  i18n   : every string via NavigationGuardStrings — zero English literals in code paths; the 4 web t()-keys
           (forms.unsavedTitle/unsavedWarning/discard/keepEditing) are preserved VERBATIM (asserted by
           testConfirmContentUsesVerbatimWebKeys + testConfirmContentFallbacks).
  a11y   : confirm prompt = combined VoiceOver label (warning + title + message); title .isHeader; every button +
           the silence toggle + the freshness chip + the backdrop labelled; reduce-motion respected (TSFadeIn);
           Dynamic Type via the Font.TS ramp.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="NavigationGuardProvider" via coordinator.start() (P1/S11), default
