STATES (every state renders — verified by previews + per-state XCTest assertions)
  loading → skeleton arming card · idle/empty → friendly "No unsaved changes" card · error → message + Retry ·
  confirming → the warning confirm card (generic OR caller message) · stale/offline → the confirm/idle card with a
  freshness chip. In production the provider is transparent (renders its children, web parity) and only `confirming`
  interrupts the user; the other states back the standalone NavigationGuardConfirmSurface presenter and are proven
  by the previews + the resolution-accessor tests (testResolutionPhaseAndAccessors). No surface is ever a blank box.

